Sometimes the codebase has a typed client (`src/api/user`) and neighbors do `vi.mock("../api/user")`. That's acceptable **only if it's the established house style** — it's a boundary the project already chose. Don't invent it just because it's easier; the default preference is still the wire-level mock.

